{"topic": "graduation rates", "review": {"readability_score": 5, "source_accuracy_score": 4, "qualification_retention_score": 4, "unsupported_claims": ["\"Ready-made 150% graduation rates ... first-time, full-time students\" with \"gender breakdowns\": the T1 sources describe rates by race/ethnicity and gender, so this is supported. The \"transfer-out rates\" claim is also supported.", "Outcome Measures: \"at degree-granting institutions\" and \"full-time and part-time, first-time and non-first-time undergraduates\" come from the table description. The example fields only cover the full-time, first-time cohort, so the cohort breadth is supported only at the table level.", "Pell/Stafford point: \"students with neither\" is supported. The 2-year/less-than-2-year scope is slightly blurred, since the source mentions less-than-2-year institutions but the topic label lists only 4-year and 2-year.", "Less-than-2-year point: \"transfer-outs\" are supported by the table definitions. \"Completers\" are also supported."], "missing_qualifications": ["The candidate omits any note that the cohort-year coverage differs by topic. It states only that reporting periods vary by data area.", "The Outcome Measures point does not say the table covers only the 2008 entering cohort. Only the 2016 outcome date is given.", "The Pell/Stafford series has a shorter period than the other areas (2016 to 2022). This is deferred to Definitions & sources, which is acceptable."], "comments": ["The candidate keeps the key qualifications: it says this is a bounded search, that cohorts and outcome dates differ, that coverage varies, and that the loan-label series are not assumed equivalent.", "The two loan-label series are described separately with an explicit non-equivalence note, which is appropriate.", "\"The same kind of aid-group graduation data\" for the Direct Subsidized series is a mild equivalence phrasing, but the later non-equivalence sentence offsets it.", "No invented dimensions were found. Most points are literally supported by the cited records."]}}
