{"topic": "faculty", "review": {"readability_score": 5, "source_accuracy_score": 5, "qualification_retention_score": 4, "unsupported_claims": [], "missing_qualifications": ["Institution coverage for the degree-granting instructional staff tables (T1, T2, T5) is not stated: the sources limit it to institutions with 15 or more full-time employees. The candidate says 'degree-granting' but omits this threshold. The final caveat that populations vary partly covers it, and the Definitions & sources panel can hold the detail.", "The Human Resources bullets do not note that salary outlays and the derived variables (T4, T6, T7) are on an academic-year basis (2015-16 to 2024-25) while other data areas are Fall. The line 'Reporting periods vary by data area' covers this without asserting uniform coverage."], "comments": ["Each narrative point matches its table definition. No invented populations, breakdowns or comparisons were found.", "T3 'split by full- or part-time and medical school status' is supported by R135859P1.", "T4 'including months-worked categories' is supported by R135860P2.", "T7 'ready-made average salaries equated to nine months... plus FTE staff by occupation' is supported by R135866P1. The nonmedical qualifier is kept.", "T8 'first-year retention' and 'institutions with undergraduate students' are supported by R135838P1 and R135838P6.", "'Reporting periods vary by data area; exact coverage is in Definitions & sources' avoids implying uniform coverage. The Fall Enrollment range of Fall 2015 through Fall 2024 is correct.", "The required qualifications (bounded search; coverage varies and availability does not guarantee reported values) are preserved.", "The answer does not claim that student-to-faculty ratio is faculty-count data, and it does not mix the Human Resources and Fall Enrollment sources."]}}
