{"topic": "expenses", "review": {"readability_score": 5, "source_accuracy_score": 4, "qualification_retention_score": 4, "unsupported_claims": ["Finance point says indicators cover \"shares of total expenses\" and \"separate indicator sets exist for different accounting standards\". The source supports these only loosely: it says expenses for salaries, wages, and benefits as a percent of total expenses, and sets of indicators for GASB, FASB and for-profit institutions. The wording is a fair paraphrase but generalizes.", "Vocational charges point says \"price of attendance with an other-expenses estimate for the largest program\". This is supported. The omission of the books and supplies and room and board components is not an error.", "\"Branch campus cost of attendance\" describes the table mainly as cost data. The table's primary content is branch location listings, with cost data provided only for branches enrolling full-time, first-time undergraduates. The candidate states this, so the framing is acceptable but slightly shifts emphasis.", "Library point calls the data \"library spending\" and \"expense distribution\". This is supported by R55P1, which describes library expenses by function and total library expenditures per FTE. It is a library-specific measure, not institution-wide expenses, and the candidate does not flag that."], "missing_qualifications": ["Institutional Characteristics reporting periods are replaced by \"vary by data area\". The exact periods are available in Definitions & sources, and the phrase does not assert uniform coverage.", "No mention that Finance indicators may include child campus data derived from parent allocation factors.", "The Academic Libraries period list mixes label formats (\"2015-16\" and \"Fiscal year 2020\") and omits the 2018-19 release, whose record reports 2017-18. This is not flagged in prose, but it is covered by the detailed catalog panel.", "No note that the Cost table's Cost of Attendance estimates cover only first-time, full-time undergraduates, while other charges apply to other groups. The candidate partly conveys this."], "comments": ["The candidate is concise, well organized and keeps both required qualifications nearly verbatim.", "No invented populations, comparisons or cohort mappings. The branch-campus \"not comprehensive\" caveat is correctly retained.", "The candidate does not claim equivalence between the sources, and the survey-level reporting periods are correct where stated.", "The main weakness is that the Finance and Libraries expense measures are described generally, so the user could mistake library expenses for institutional expenses. The point titles do distinguish them, which limits the concern."]}}
