{"topic": "institution characteristics", "review": {"readability_score": 3, "source_accuracy_score": 4, "qualification_retention_score": 4, "unsupported_claims": ["\"The latest mission statement table\" for the seventh series: the sources do not establish that 2023-24 is the latest mission statement table. This is a mild implication, and the 2024-25 directory exists without a matching mission table.", "\"Active status is also flagged in this directory\" is supported only loosely. The source says it identifies institutions as currently active Title IV participants, and the candidate drops that Title IV context."], "missing_qualifications": ["The first mission series is described only as \"one group of years\". It covers 2015-16, 2017-18 and 2018-19, but the narrative does not say that it is non-contiguous.", "The series are not tied to specific years in the prose. The ordinal labels (second to seventh) do not show that the second series is 2016-17, and the single-year entries do not say which year each one covers. These details sit in the linked coverage panel.", "The directory's period range (2015-16 to 2024-25, with 2024-25 provisional) is not stated in the prose. This is acceptable because \"periods vary\" is stated and the details are linked.", "The candidate keeps the three required qualifications, but drops the template's closing statement that these are codebook and table matches rather than confirmation of reported values. The required availability caveat still covers this."], "comments": ["Directory fields (names, locations, URLs, sector, control, level, Carnegie) are supported by the T1 records, including the sector variable definition.", "Mission statement descriptions (statement text or URL) match the table definitions in every series.", "The ordinal labels (\"first\" to \"seventh\") and the repetitive wording are unhelpful for readability. Year-based labels or a merged description would be clearer, as long as it did not claim the series are equivalent.", "The candidate does not assert uniform coverage. \"Reporting periods vary by data area\" is acceptable, and the source series are kept separate with the reason given.", "No invented breakdowns or populations were found."]}}
