{"topic": "academic libraries", "review": {"readability_score": 5, "source_accuracy_score": 4, "qualification_retention_score": 4, "unsupported_claims": ["\"Expenditure data apply to those with higher total expenditures\" is a loose paraphrase of \"total expenditures over $100,000\"; it is directionally supported but the threshold is dropped.", "\"Tuition, required fees and per credit hour charges ... for institutions reporting academic-year charges\" is supported by the record text. The IC record also covers price of attendance and professional-practice charges, which the summary omits. This is an omission, not an unsupported claim."], "missing_qualifications": ["The Academic Libraries reporting periods are listed with mixed labels (2019-20, then Fiscal year 2020), and the source labels differ across years. The candidate repeats the list as given without flagging the change.", "The Academic Libraries source records show the 2018-19 release (AL2018) as a separate table, but the period list omits it. The candidate does not note this gap.", "The Cost topic covers only 2024-25 provisional data. The candidate states the period but does not say the data are provisional.", "The race/ethnicity by gender HR table notes that reporting was optional in even-numbered years before 2016. The candidate does not mention this, though it appears in the linked source records."], "comments": ["The wording is concise and readable, and the required bounded-search and coverage-varies qualifications are kept.", "There are no invented dimensions, populations or measure types. Descriptions of each data area match the source text.", "\"Reporting periods vary by data area\" for Human Resources does not assert uniform coverage, and the exact periods are available in Definitions & sources.", "\"Months-worked categories\" is supported by the SAL records.", "\"Including a librarian-related category\" is supported by the SANIN04 and SANIT04 variable definitions.", "The Library \"collection and spending indicators\" description matches the DRVAL table text, including the per-FTE-enrollment expenditure measure."]}}
